# Vauxhall 14/40 two-seater with dickey, 1922-1927.
#
# The 14/40: announced in October 1921 and renamed the 14/40 in October 1923,
# the M-type of 1922 becoming the LM-type from late 1924. It is unrelated to
# the post-war 14 hp of 1948. The open two-seater with a dickey seat is
# modelled, which is the body the photograph shows.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_14-40
#
# Dimensions: length 4.200 m (166 in), wheelbase 3.000 m (117 in). A period
# road test gives 2.896 m for the early M-type and 2.972 m for the later car;
# the conflict is recorded. No overall width or height was found and both are
# estimated from the photograph.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. The side image is
# about 35-40 degrees off a true side at waist height, so the flank is a
# reasoned estimate and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Dark Green,
# Maroon and Grey are period finishes. Weights 10, 9, 8, 7, total 34,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 100 km/h. Comfort 30/375, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 30. Classes 2,3,4.
# Dates: intro January 1922; retires staggered 1938-1942 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-14-40.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-14-40.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-14-40/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the width, height and flank are estimated from a side
# view about 35-40 degrees off the axis. The rear profile and the closed dickey
# lid are inferred. The 3.000 m wheelbase is the published figure and is not
# verified for this car, a period road test giving 2.896 m for the early
# M-type.


